ent migrations to probe-based transport selection (explicit URL/env override wins, then the `[<role>] transport` config preference, then probe: socket file exists + connect succeeds -> UDS, else TCP — the dispatch client's probe-then-choose pattern, `crates/fleet-dispatch/src/lib.rs:152-183`):\n- queue client direct path (`crates/fleet-queue/src/client.rs:69-84,100-113`)\n- queue-broker's `DirectSecrets` hop to secrets-broker (`crates/fleet-queue/src/queue_broker.rs:48-51,604-605`) — gains a `unix://` form or sibling `secrets_socket` setting\n- laptop-local `fleet secrets` path\n- On the way past: fix the queue client's hardcoded broker-sock path (`client.rs:55-57`) to ask `fleet-config` instead.\n\nSandbox consumers are untouched — they speak UDS to their local proxy, a different socket.\n\n## Acceptance\n- Each migrated client works over UDS when the role socket answers and falls back to TCP when it does not.\n- No behavior change when only TCP is configured.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- Fleet clients select UDS vs TCP per role by probing, with no manual configuration.\n- A failed or absent socket probe falls back to TCP within the same connection attempt.\n- Probe behavior is covered by tests for socket-present, socket-absent, and socket-stale cases.\n","closed_by":{"login":"developing-today[bot]","id":347365078,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOFLRe1g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/26439447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/developing-today","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today%5Bbot%5D/